  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_56b1f27c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black man in a kitchen, eating a banana while looking intently at a laptop, with text overlay that reads 'when they say not to blink or you'll miss the magic trick.' The scene is framed to suggest he is intensely focused on something on the screen, possibly a video or trick. The meme's intent is to humorously portray the experience of being so engrossed in something that one forgets to blink, using the man's focused expression as the visual punchline. While the image itself does not contain overtly abusive, hateful, or cyberbullying content, it relies on a racialized stereotype by using a Black man as the subject of a common 'not blinking' trope. This can be considered harmful because it reinforces the stereotype that Black people are hyper-focused or 'always watching,' which can contribute to racial profiling or the perpetuation of negative racial tropes. The meme's humor is derived from the juxtaposition of the mundane (eating a banana) with the intense focus required to 'not blink,' but the racialized subject matter can be seen as a subtle form of racial stereotyping, which is a form of harmful content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6b2bceab"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
